  "courseName": "Human Anatomy and Physiology I",
  "estimatedLength": "35 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify and name the four chambers of the heart: right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium, and left ventricle.",
    "Identify the four heart valves and the major vessels entering and leaving the heart, including the venae cavae, pulmonary arteries and veins, and aorta.",
    "Trace the ordered pathway of blood through the heart's pulmonary and systemic circuits using correct anatomical terminology.",
    "Distinguish pulmonary circulation from systemic circulation and explain why the right and left sides of the heart serve different circulatory roles.",
    "Relate the thicker myocardium of the left ventricle to the higher pressure required to pump blood through systemic circulation.",
    "Describe how atrioventricular and semilunar valves prevent backflow during the cardiac cycle."
  ],
